Optional: an S3 bucket (for artifacts) or an ECR repository (for Docker images).

Quick concept recap
CodeBuild runs a build using a YAML file called buildspec.yml (by default CodeBuild looks for it at repo root). You can also define buildspec directly in the console. 
AWS Documentation

Option A — Build JAR and upload to S3 (step-by-step)
1) Add buildspec.yml to repo (root)
Create buildspec.yml in your project root (example for Maven + Java 17):

version: 0.2

env:
  variables:
    MAVEN_OPTS: "-Xmx1024m"

phases:
  install:
    runtime-versions:
      java: corretto17
    commands:
      - echo "Installing dependencies (mvn will download dependencies)"
  pre_build:
    commands:
      - echo "Pre-build step (optional)"
  build:
    commands:
      - echo "Build started on `date`"
      - mvn -B clean package
  post_build:
    commands:
      - echo "Build completed on `date`"
artifacts:
  files:
    - target/*.jar
  discard-paths: yes
Notes:

runtime-versions ensures CodeBuild uses a runtime with Java (you can override image in the console). 
AWS Documentation

2) Create (or choose) an S3 bucket for artifacts
You can use the console or CLI:

aws s3 mb s3://my-spring-artifacts-12345 --region us-east-1
3) Create a CodeBuild service role (IAM)
In IAM console: Roles → Create role → AWS service → CodeBuild (service principal codebuild.amazonaws.com) and attach the minimal policies your build needs. AWS docs cover this process. 
AWS Documentation

Minimal example policy (attach to the role) — replace your-bucket-name:

{
  "Version": "2012-10-17",
  "Statement": [
    {
      "Effect": "Allow",
      "Action": [
        "s3:PutObject",
        "s3:GetObject",
        "s3:PutObjectAcl",
        "s3:GetBucketLocation"
      ],
      "Resource": [
        "arn:aws:s3:::your-bucket-name/*"
      ]
    },
    {
      "Effect": "Allow",
      "Action": [
        "logs:CreateLogGroup",
        "logs:CreateLogStream",
        "logs:PutLogEvents"
      ],
      "Resource": "arn:aws:logs:*:*:*"
    }
  ]
}
(You can attach AmazonS3FullAccess while learning, but in production restrict to the specific bucket.) 
AWS Documentation

4) Create the CodeBuild Project (console)
Open CodeBuild → Create build project and fill:

Project name: springboot-build

Source provider: GitHub (or CodeCommit). Connect your repo / set repository URL and branch.

Environment:

Environment image: Managed image

Operating system: Amazon Linux 2 (or Ubuntu) — default is fine

Runtime(s): You can leave image and use the runtime-versions in buildspec (recommended).

Service role: Choose the IAM role you created (or let CodeBuild create one).

Buildspec: Use the buildspec in the source (default) — it will run the buildspec.yml in the repo root.

Artifacts: Amazon S3 → choose the S3 bucket and specify an output name (or keep default).

Save/Create. The console flow is described in AWS "Getting started" docs. 
AWS Documentation

5) Trigger a build (manual)
In CodeBuild console, select project → Start build.

Watch logs stream in the console (CloudWatch Logs are created automatically).

Or automate with CodePipeline (see later).

Option B — Build Docker image and push to ECR (step-by-step)
This flow is for when you containerize Spring Boot and deploy to ECS/EKS.

1) Create ECR repo
aws ecr create-repository --repository-name springboot-app --region us-east-1
2) buildspec.yml to build & push Docker image (example)
This is based on AWS sample for publishing to ECR. It logs in, builds, tags, and pushes. 
AWS Documentation

version: 0.2

env:
  variables:
    IMAGE_REPO_NAME: "springboot-app"
    IMAGE_TAG: "latest"
phases:
  pre_build:
    commands:
      - echo Logging in to Amazon ECR...
      - aws --version
      - $(aws ecr get-login-password --region $AWS_DEFAULT_REGION | docker login --username AWS --password-stdin <your-account-id>.dkr.ecr.$AWS_DEFAULT_REGION.amazonaws.com)
      - REPO_URI=<your-account-id>.dkr.ecr.$AWS_DEFAULT_REGION.amazonaws.com/$IMAGE_REPO_NAME
  build:
    commands:
      - echo Building the Docker image...
      - docker build -t $IMAGE_REPO_NAME:$IMAGE_TAG .
      - docker tag $IMAGE_REPO_NAME:$IMAGE_TAG $REPO_URI:$IMAGE_TAG
  post_build:
    commands:
      - echo Pushing the Docker image...
      - docker push $REPO_URI:$IMAGE_TAG
artifacts:
  files: []
Notes:

Replace <your-account-id> and set AWS_DEFAULT_REGION as environment variable in the project (or use CodeBuild environment variable settings).

The CodeBuild service role must be allowed to call ecr:GetAuthorizationToken, ecr:BatchCheckLayerAvailability, ecr:PutImage, and ecr:InitiateLayerUpload etc.; the AWS docs have the exact permission list. 
AWS Documentation

